PU Learning for Response Selection
==================================

This repository contains the reference implementation for the paper
"Positive-Unlabeled Learning for Response Selection".

It builds on, and redistributes code from, the following projects.


1. BERT-FP (Fine-grained Post-training for Improving Retrieval-based
   Dialogue Systems)
   --------------------------------------------------------------------
   Janghoon Han, Taesuk Hong, Byoungjae Kim, Youngjoong Ko, Jungyun Seo.
   NAACL-HLT 2021.
   Source: https://github.com/hanjanghoon/BERT_FP

   The post-training stage (FPT/), the fine-tuning stage
   (FineTuning/Response_selection.py, FineTuning/Metrics.py,
   FineTuning/BERT_finetuning/) and the data pipeline (Data_processing.py)
   are derived from that repository and modified to support the
   positive-unlabeled setting described in our paper.


2. PU_learning (Mixture Proportion Estimation and PU Learning:
   A Modern Approach)
   --------------------------------------------------------------------
   Saurabh Garg, Yifan Wu, Alex Smola, Sivaraman Balakrishnan,
   Zachary C. Lipton. NeurIPS 2021.
   Source: https://github.com/acmi-lab/PU_learning
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

   The mixture-proportion-estimation baselines in PvU/estimators/
   (EN_estimator.py, scott.py, KM.py, TIcE.py, dedpul.py, dedpulUtils.py)
   are taken from that repository. BBE_estimator.py is adapted from its
   estimator.py.

   A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is included in LICENSE.
